+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+After physical MAIN authorization, engagement and target/actual speeds of at least 30 km/h must persist for 0.5 seconds before a SET− request. The same conditions apply after optional low-target cancellation.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+After turning ON, restart and operate MAIN physically. Brake, CANCEL, MAIN OFF or observation gaps revoke authorization; cycle MAIN OFF then ON to rearm. OFF inhibits new requests without cancelling already engaged cruise.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Below 30 km/h actual speed, the driver must accelerate. No direct braking or launch from standstill; stock-vehicle acceptance of the new path remains unvalidated.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
